# Commit scope

One commit is one capability. Do not put unrelated work in the same commit.

- Include only files and edits that serve the same feature, fix, or refactor.
- If the working tree has more than one independent change (for example dashboard and official holidays), make a separate commit for each.
- A shared helper belongs with the feature that introduced it. If two unrelated features both need it, commit the helper first, then each feature.
- Do not stage leftover edits, formatting, or generated files that are not part of that capability.
- If the user asked to commit everything, still split by capability and say how many commits you will make.

# Commit messages

Apply only when the user asked to commit, or a plan todo is a commit. Do not draft this format while coding.

**Subject:** one imperative line that states why. Match existing history. No `feat:` / `fix:` prefix.

**Body:** blank line after the subject, then only sections that have items:

- Added — new behavior or path
- Changed — existing behavior that changed
- Removed — something taken out
- Fixed — a bug

Each section is a heading plus `-` bullets. Omit empty sections.

```
Point the admin account menu at the logged-in employer so staff can edit their own profile from the header.

Changed:
- Wire Profile to admin.employers.edit for the authenticated employer

Removed:
- Drop Memberships, Orders, and Inbox placeholders until those screens exist

Added:
- Cover the account dropdown in the admin navbar unit tests
```
